  SELECT 'listening-p2-set018-q001' AS sk, '{"correct_option":"A"}'::jsonb AS correct_answer, '{"transcript":"**Segment 1 — It saves time**\n\nThursday used to vanish into errands. I would leave work, in traffic, search three shops for one item, and reach home too late to cook. Now I order household basics from my phone while waiting for a meeting to start. Last week I bought printer ink in under two minutes, whereas finding the right cartridge in town once took an entire afternoon. Convenience matters, but the hours I get back are the real reason I shop this way.\n\n\n\n**Segment 2 — It is cheaper**\n\nI wanted a pair of running shoes, but the sports shop price made me put them straight back on the shelf. That evening I found the same model online, added a seasonal code, and paid twenty-five pounds less. I usually check delivery costs and return policies because a supposed bargain can become expensive. Still, comparing several sellers on one screen makes it much easier to spot a genuine deal, and my budget benefits from that.\n\n\n\n**Segment 3 — Products are delivered**\n\nBuying a bookshelf sounds simple until you try carrying one onto a crowded bus. I learned that lesson with a small desk and promised myself never again. These days, bulky orders arrive at the entrance to my building, and the driver even calls if I am not home. I could probably find some items slightly cheaper in town, but avoiding the lifting and transport is worth more to me. The doorstep service is the advantage I notice most.\n\n\n\n**Segment 4 — There are more choices**\n\nMy feet are an awkward size: one shop may have the right length but only in black, while another has bright colours in every size except mine. Online, I can search dozens of brands and filter by size, material, and style before I look at the price. Sometimes the amount of choice becomes overwhelming, and I open far too many tabs. Even so, I would rather compare twenty suitable pairs than settle for the only pair left on a local shelf.","transcript_status":"source_word_comments","word_comment_ids":["354","355","356","357"],"speaker_labels":["Person A","Person B","Person C","Person D"]}'::jsonb AS solution_data
  UNION ALL
