  UNION ALL
  SELECT 'listening-p2-set031-q001' AS sk, '{"correct_option":"A"}'::jsonb AS correct_answer, '{"transcript":"**Segment 1 — in the fitness centre**\n\nThe weather forecast used to decide whether I exercised. Heat, rain, or darkness each provided a good excuse. Then I joined a centre near the station. Inside, I can choose a treadmill, set a precise pace, and move straight to strength training afterwards. I miss outdoor scenery sometimes, but consistency matters more. A controlled indoor space means the session happens regardless of what is falling from the sky.\n\n\n\n**Segment 2 — at the seaside**\n\nI leave my shoes beside the door and start just before sunrise. The promenade is nearly empty, fishing boats are returning, and the air smells of salt. On calm days I run on firm sand; when the tide is high, I use the path above the beach. Hills might improve my fitness more , but the sea makes me want to go out, and that is what sustains a routine.\n\n\n\n**Segment 3 — in the street**\n\nThere is a park fifteen minutes away, yet travelling there makes a short run feel like an expedition. I prefer stepping outside and beginning immediately. My route uses residential roads, a shopping street before it gets busy, and a hill near the station. I wear reflective clothing and avoid rush hour because cars are the obvious disadvantage. Even so, the convenience of running through my own streets keeps the habit simple.\n\n\n\n**Segment 4 — on the running track**\n\nI am training for ten kilometres and need honest numbers. GPS can lose signal beneath trees, but the stadium lane never changes: twenty-five laps means ten kilometres. The surface is forgiving, there are no traffic lights, and I can leave water beside the start line. Scenic routes are more enjoyable, but when I am testing pace or racing a friend, measured laps on the track are far more useful.","transcript_status":"source_word_comments","word_comment_ids":["406","407","408","409"],"speaker_labels":["Person A","Person B","Person C","Person D"]}'::jsonb AS solution_data
  UNION ALL
