  SELECT 'listening-p2-set042-q001' AS sk, '{"correct_option":"A"}'::jsonb AS correct_answer, '{"transcript":"**Segment 1 — read when travelling to school**\n\nI used to read a lot in my bedroom when I was younger, especially before going to sleep. But these days, I don''t really read at home anymore because my phone is always next to me. The only time I read properly is on the bus in the morning. My journey to school takes about thirty minutes, so I usually bring a novel with me and read a few pages before class.\n\n\n\n**Segment 2 — don''t have time to read**\n\nI actually enjoy books, and I''ve got two new ones on my desk right now. Sometimes I even put one beside my bed, thinking I''ll read it before I sleep. But most evenings I''m too tired after homework, football practice, and helping my parents. On weekends, I often plan to read, but something else always comes up. So, at the moment, I hardly read at all.\n\n\n\n**Segment 3 — read on their beds**\n\nSome of my friends read on the train or bus, but I can''t do that because it makes me feel a bit sick. I also don''t like reading in the living room because the TV is usually on. For me, the best place is my bed. I read there almost every night, even if it''s only for ten minutes. It helps me relax and forget about school for a while.\n\n\n\n**Segment 4 — prefer another activity to reading books**\n\nMy parents keep telling me that reading is important, and I agree with them, really. I sometimes read short stories for school, and I can finish them if I have to. But when I have free time, I''d much rather play basketball or watch videos about sports. Books are okay, but they don''t excite me as much as doing something active with my friends.","transcript_status":"source_word_comments","word_comment_ids":["450","451","452","453"],"speaker_labels":["Person A","Person B","Person C","Person D"]}'::jsonb AS solution_data
  UNION ALL
