re. Competition can sometimes lead to universities focusing too much on rankings and flashy features instead of the of education. It can become more about marketing than genuine improvement.\nM: That''s a fair concern. But competition also forces universities to constantly improve, which can benefit students in the long run.","transcript_status":"source_word_comment","word_comment_ids":["467"],"speaker_labels":["Man","Woman"]}'::jsonb AS solution_data
