  SELECT 'listening-p3-set026-q001' AS sk, '{"correct_option":"man"}'::jsonb AS correct_answer, '{"transcript":"W: Our building committee wants a greenhouse on the roof, and the architect has brought three designs for tonight''s meeting.\nM: Before we admire drawings, remember that the city lacks affordable homes. Housing space is more important than farming space, even if rooftop gardens sound fashionable.\nW: This roof cannot legally support apartments, but it can support lightweight growing beds. The best design includes trees, seating, and a small market, so it would make the block far more attractive.\nM: I doubt a greenhouse would make the building more attractive for long; poorly maintained beds could look worse than the empty roof.\nW: The cooperative would sell herbs to cafés and employ two residents. It could help the local economy as well as reduce food transport.\nM: Two jobs are not an economic revolution.\nW: No, and the greenhouse will not solve food shortages by itself.\nM: On that we agree. A roof cannot feed an entire district.\nW: It can still demonstrate one practical use for wasted space.\nM: As long as nobody presents it as a substitute for housing or rural agriculture.\nW: Then the proposal should describe it as a small local supplement, not a miracle cure. **Explanation summary** *User-provided Part 3 topic version for Urban Farming ( version 4 ). Check the statement-level explanations for the final speaker mapping.*","transcript_status":"source_word_comment","word_comment_ids":["486"],"speaker_labels":["Man","Woman"]}'::jsonb AS solution_data
  UNION ALL
