  SELECT 'listening-p3-set042-q001' AS sk, '{"correct_option":"woman"}'::jsonb AS correct_answer, '{"transcript":"W: I understand why home education appeals to some parents. In a large class, even a good teacher has to move at a pace that suits most pupils. At home, a child can spend longer on difficult subjects and move faster through material they already understand.\nM: That may improve academic progress, but I worry about what happens beyond lessons. School teaches children to cooperate, manage disagreements, and build relationships with people from different backgrounds. A weekly sports club may help, but it is not the same as spending every day with classmates.\nW: Perhaps, although homeschooled children are not automatically isolated. They can join music groups, community projects, and online classes. A flexible timetable can also support children with health conditions, families who travel, or young people training seriously in sport.\nM: Flexibility is useful, but parents need time, patience, and enough subject knowledge. Good intentions do not always produce effective teaching.\nW: I agree. I would not present homeschooling as a solution for every household.\nM: Nor would I reject it completely. Its success depends on the child''s needs, the support available, and the of the education.","transcript_status":"source_word_comment","word_comment_ids":["502"],"speaker_labels":["Man","Woman"]}'::jsonb AS solution_data
  UNION ALL
